Skippy Wallet is a fork of the Paradym Wallet, taken at commit
2d68168863dd8e78f883b752f420dc46aa2d7108 (2026-07-22) of the upstream `main`
branch.

Modifications made by Skippy, as required by section 4(b) of the Apache License:

  - Rebranded from Paradym Wallet to Skippy Wallet: application name, bundle
    identifiers, URL scheme, icons, splash screens, copy and legal links.
  - Added a build-time multi-brand system (apps/wallet/brands) so the wallet can
    be shipped under different brands from one codebase.
  - Added runtime tenant branding resolved from the Skippy hub
    (apps/wallet/src/brand).
  - Removed the demo trust anchors shipped upstream and replaced the trust
    configuration with Skippy's own.
  - Disabled DIDComm, over-asking AI analysis and the cloud HSM integration.
  - Replaced Animo-hosted service endpoints and support contacts with Skippy's.
  - Replaced the CI and release configuration.

A per-file record of intentional divergence from upstream is kept in
docs/REBRAND.md.

